# BINTRANS autonomous scope

Work only in `D:\Projects\freight-platform-staging-pack` on branch `ops/bintrans-ct-staging-pack` unless the operator directs otherwise.

This repository may be worked on autonomously for local development, static analysis, tests, documentation, and **local commits**.

Any action that changes remote infrastructure, staging runtime, database, registry, protected secrets, production, Control Tower primary mode, or remote Git state requires explicit operator authorization.

## Autonomous (local, no prompt expected when Run Mode + allowlists are active)

- Repository inspection: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`, `git branch`, `grep`, `rg`
- Static validation: `bash -n`, offline `*_selfcheck.sh`, `docker compose config`
- Local tests: `go test`, `go vet`, applicable `npm` scripts
- Edits under this worktree; `git add` + `git commit` when requested

## Stop at live gates (require operator approval)

- VM update / SSH
- JWT_SECRET provisioning
- Registry login / push / live digest collection
- `docker compose up` (runtime or observability)
- Cohort approval / Day 0 observation
- `CONTROL_TOWER_READ_MODEL_MODE=primary`
- `git push`, merge, force push

## Never autonomous

- Rerun migration (schema already at version 19)
- Create cohort manifests or fabricate tenant IDs
- Touch production or old shared VPS
- Modify `/protected/` staging env or print secrets
